        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/slendertroll/{size}/2832_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-03-16T05:42:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>[quote=““Greonhal””]</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"SlenderTroll\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/slendertroll/48/2832_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> SlenderTroll:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think Baron Blade in any environment <span class=\"bbcode-i\">except</span> Mars is confusing. Wouldn’t he kill himself if he crashed the moon into his own planet?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>See, Baron Blade <span class=\"bbcode-i\">on</span> Mars confuses me. Is he dropping Phobos and/or Demos on the heroes? If he succeeds in dropping the moon, why does everyone just stop, otherwise? They could be rationalizing that humanity’s down to the 3-6 of them, I suppose, but would that necessarily stop, for example, the vendetta between Blade and Legacy?<br>\n[/quote]He’s dropping the Moon on Earth, which would wipe out all life. After that, the heroes could probably still beat him up, but what’s the point, really? Blade has won, and the heroes, tasked with guarding the population of Earth from evildoers, have failed.</p>",
